      "problem": "Simplify the expression $6a+1-2a.$",
      "worked_solution": "We rearrange the terms so that the like terms, $6a$ and $-2a$, are together.\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t6a+1-2a &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\underbrace{6a-2a}_{a \\textrm{ terms}}+ 1\t&\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we combine the like terms: \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\underbrace{6a-2a}+ 1 &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t(6-2)a + 1 &=\\[5pt]\n\t\t4a + 1&\t\t\n\t}\n$$",
